00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.680
Hey it's Joey and welcome to Better Ideas.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:13.269
You've probably heard the news - cold showers
are the secret to unlocking your inner potential

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:15.900
and giving you super powers beyond your wildest
dreams.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.150
Now, there are a ton of YouTube videos and
articles online that you can find that get

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.450
into the nitty-gritty of exactly what cold
showers do to you physiologically but what

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.570
I'm more interested in is what they do to
you mentally.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.590
I actually gave a speech about cold showers
last semester for a public speaking class.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.740
Joey: "It's almost like your primal brain
thinks you're being tossed into a river from

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.960
your slumber or something - you're fighting
for your life basically."

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.391
I talked about the physiological benefits
as well as my own experience with the 30 day

00:00:43.391 --> 00:00:44.800
cold shower challenge.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.050
Now before we dive into what I find is the
most fascinating part, which is the mental

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:52.550
benefit of cold showers, let's just do a quick
review of the physical benefits, in case you're

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.550
uninitiated.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.310
Medical Daily says, "cold shower refined skin
and hair and rehydrates it."

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.190
Makes sense, because, I mean I don't know
if you've ever taken a really really hot,

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.720
long, steamy shower before - you probably
have if you're human - often your hair gets

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.120
really dried out and your skin starts to ash
or you get ashy elbows or something.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.880
Anyways, cold showers will stop that.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.070
The Art of Manliness says that according to
a study done by the Thrombosis Research Centre

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:20.500
back in 1993, individuals who took daily cold
showers saw an increase in the number of virus-fighting

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.080
white blood cells compared to individuals
who took hot showers.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.080
Cool stuff.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.240
Still not the coolest part, though.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.280
LifeHack says that a third benefit is that
it stimulates brown fat, which is the good

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.930
fat in your body, apparently that a lot of
people don't know about.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.650
So, the fat that you're trying to get rid
of is called yellow fat, and it's the bad,

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:41.060
undesirable fat that usually collects around
your waistline and your tummy.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.220
Tummy...

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.380
Stomach.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.360
Brown fat helps to eat away at bad or yellow
fat.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.950
So basically, cold showers stimulate weight-loss,
which is awesome.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.200
Now there are a ton of other benefits, that
people claim cold showers are responsible

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:58.820
for, like increased fertility in men, increased
testosterone in men... a lot of "Men Benefits".

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.730
and mitigating symptoms of depressions.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:04.200
Now all these benefits sound like enough reason
to take a cold shower right now, and they

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.380
probably are, but I find - the coolest part
about cold showers is what they do to you

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:10.390
as a person.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.510
Which kinda sounds like fluffy stuff, but
let me break it down for you: First of all,

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.810
going back to the concept of The Flinch, which
I talked about in an earlier video, I'll put

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.150
the link in the description - cold showers
are extremely uncomfortable.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.980
Even the mere thought of having to take one
makes you uncomfortable.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.940
Despite the fact that you have absolutely
nothing to lose except your comfort, and all

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.020
those benefits to gain.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.099
Now think about all the things that you're
really proud of in life - the things that

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:33.129
you put blood, sweat, and tears into achieving.

00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:36.020
How many hours of discomfort did you put into
achieving those things?

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:39.260
But standing here in the present day, aren't
you glad you went through that anyways?

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.910
Because the pain is gone now - and all that's
remaining is the result of your discomfort,

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.420
hard work, and perseverance.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.640
So in a way, cold showers are the ultimate
brain hack, and it forces you right off the

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.390
get-go to get into a no pain, no gain mentality.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:54.990
It forces you to scare away the flinch right
when you wake up, so that when it comes time

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.950
to do schoolwork, laundry, fill out your taxes
- it's absolutely nothing - you'll just go

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.670
and do it - there is no flinch anymore - you've
scared it away.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:05.620
All of these little tasks that you usually
don't end up doing seem like nothing in comparison

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.240
to the cold shower you took that morning.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.470
You've conditioned yourself to be comfortable
with the uncomfortable - and you've shifted

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:15.110
your brain's mentaility from instant gratification
and momentary pleasure to long-term gain,

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.210
and real, substantial benefit - and that's
why cold showers are so powerful.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.370
So I challenge you - go take a cold shower
today.

